\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I Dared not hope that Thou, wouldst deign to come
\par And make this lowly heart of mine Thy home,
\par That Thou wouldst deign, O King of kings, to be
\par E'en for one hour a sojourner in me:
\par Yet art Thou always here to help, and bless,
\par And lift the load of my great sinfulness.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I dared not ever hope for such a Guide
\par To walk with with me my faltering steps beside,
\par To help me when I fall, and, when I stray,
\par Constrain me gently to the better way;
\par Yet art Thou always at my side to be
\par A Counsellor and comforter to me
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I do not always go where thou dost lead
\par I do not always thy soft whispers heed
\par I follow other light and in my sin
\par I vex with many a slight my friend within
\par Yet dost thou not through grieved from me depart
\par But guardest still thy place within my heart\f1 
\par 
\par }

